IMPORT prelude

-- Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 (Cth), Chapter 4 (medical devices), as it meets a patient who has had a medical device
-- implanted or applied in treatment (a pelvic mesh, a breast implant, a hip) and is weighing a claim about it.
--
-- SEAT: the patient. Every exported question is phrased as that person would ask it: "Is my implant a medical device?",
-- "Is this company the sponsor of my device?", "Was my device covered by the Register when it was supplied to me?",
-- "What does the supplier face for supplying it?", "Can they be made to recall it or warn about it?", "Did the sponsor
-- report what it knew in time?", "Must the hospital report what happened to me?". The Act gives the patient no right to
-- sue; it decides who the sponsor and manufacturer are, whether the supply was lawful, and what the sponsor had to tell
-- the regulator and by when. Those are the facts a claim under other law (negligence, the Australian Consumer Law, a class
-- action) builds on. Section 41KE says Part 4-9 does not "exclude or limit the operation of any other law".
--
-- Where the Act hands a matter to the Secretary ("the Secretary is satisfied", "it appears to the Secretary"), to a court,
-- or to the regulations (the essential principles, reportable devices, reporting periods, exempt devices), the answer is
-- conditional on it, asked as a fact.
--
-- Provisions covered: s 3(1) ("sponsor", "supply", "healthcare facility", "reportable medical device", "exempt device"),
-- ss 41BD, 41BF, 41BG, 41BH (as a comment), 41FM, 41FN(3)(d), 41GI, 41GQ (as dates asked), 41HC(6B), (6E), (6FA),
-- 41JM, 41KA, 41KC, 41KCA, 41MA(5), (8), (8A), 41MAA(2), 41MB, 41MI, 41MIB, 41MK (as a comment), 41MP, 41MPA, 41GN(1)(d);
-- Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 36(1) item 6 and s 36(2) (Saturdays and Sundays only) for the periods.
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 89 (register id C2025C00525), compilation date 5 September 2025, includes amendments up to Act
-- No. 38, 2025, deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A03952.txt (retrieved 13 October 2026). The compiled
-- text is applied to every date from 4 October 2002, when Chapter 4 began; earlier compilations are not deposited, so a
-- supply years ago is judged by today's text (NOTES.md). The Therapeutic Goods (Medical Devices) Regulations 2002 are
-- not deposited: the essential principles, the reporting periods, reportable devices and exempt devices are INPUTS.
-- Penalties are in penalty units; the value of a penalty unit (Crimes Act 1914 s 4AA) is not used.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the
-- individual to whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 (Cth), Chapter 4: medical devices, from the seat of the patient`

§§ `Dates and periods`

-- Built-in date functions only (no daydate), so nothing here collides with a library's YMD.
GIVEN `d` IS A NUMBER, `m` IS A NUMBER, `y` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` `d` `m` `y` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY `d` `m` `y`

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`day number of` `the day` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the day`

GIVEN `a` IS A DATE, `b` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is on or after` `a` `b` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `a` AT LEAST DATE_SERIAL `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A DATE, `b` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is before` `a` `b` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `a` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `b`

GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`n` `days after` `the day` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the day` PLUS `n`)

-- 1 January 1990 was a Monday; days 5 and 6 of each week counted from it are Saturday and Sunday.
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`falls on a Saturday or Sunday` `the day` MEANS
    ((DATE_SERIAL `the day` MINUS DATE_SERIAL (`the date` 1 1 1990)) MODULO 7) AT LEAST 5

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 36(2): if "the last day for doing the thing is a Saturday, a Sunday or a holiday ...
-- the thing may be done on the next day that is not a Saturday, a Sunday or a holiday". Public holidays (s 36(3)) are
-- not counted here: they depend on the place, and no holiday law is read (NOTES.md).
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`moved off a weekend` `the day` MEANS
    IF `falls on a Saturday or Sunday` `the day`
    THEN `moved off a weekend` (1 `days after` `the day`)
    ELSE `the day`

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 36(1) item 6: a period "expressed to begin after a specified day ... does not include
-- that day" (Example 6: 28 days after 2 August begins on 3 August). So the last day of "within N days after" a day is
-- that day plus N, moved off a weekend.
GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of` `n` `days after` `the day` MEANS `moved off a weekend` (`n` `days after` `the day`)

-- Endnotes: Therapeutic Goods Amendment (Medical Devices) Act 2002 (No. 24, 2002), "Sch 1: 4 Oct 2002". Chapter 4 as a
-- whole is "ad. No. 24, 2002".
`the day Chapter 4 began` MEANS `the date` 4 10 2002

§§ `The duties with deadlines, as regulative rules`

DECLARE `Device party` IS ONE OF
    `the sponsor`
    `the health practitioner`

DECLARE `Device act` IS ONE OF
    `give the information to the Secretary`
    `notify the supply to the Secretary`

-- ss 41FN(3)(d), 41MP(1), 41MPA(1): the person in relation to whom the kind of device is included in the Register must
-- give information of a s 41MP(2) kind to the Secretary "within the period specified in the regulations". The timeline is
-- in day numbers; the rule starts on the day the sponsor came to know of the information (the regulations count from
-- awareness; they are not deposited, so the start and the period are both asked).
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Device party` `Device act`
`ss 41MP, 41MPA -- the sponsor must give the information to the Secretary within the period in the regulations` MEANS
    PARTY `the sponsor`
    MUST  `give the information to the Secretary`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the sponsor` BECAUSE "s 41MP(1): an offence if the sponsor knew, up to 12 months or 1,000 penalty units; s 41MPA(1): civil penalty up to 3,000 penalty units (individual) or 30,000 (body corporate); s 41GN(1)(d): a ground to cancel the entry"

-- s 41HC(6B): a person authorised by s 41HC(6) rules who supplies a device under them "must (c) notify the supply to the
-- Secretary; and (d) do so within 28 days after the supply". The rule starts on the day of the supply.
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Device party` `Device act`
`s 41HC(6B) -- the health practitioner must notify the supply within 28 days after it` MEANS
    PARTY `the health practitioner`
    MUST  `notify the supply to the Secretary`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the health practitioner` BECAUSE "s 41HC(6E): an offence of strict liability (s 41HC(6F)), 10 penalty units"

DECLARE `Done in time or not` IS ONE OF
    `there is no such duty on these facts`
    `done in time`
    `not done in time`
    `still open until` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE

-- Not a provision of the Act: the helper that runs a rule over what happened. On the stable l4 a CONSIDER on an
-- EVALTRACE can match FULFILLED, and OTHERWISE takes a breach and a rule still waiting alike. So where the act has been
-- done, FULFILLED means in time; where it has not, the helper asks whether doing it today would still keep the rule.
-- An act dated before the rule starts is settled by the callers from the dates, not here.
GIVEN `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Device party` `Device act`
      `the party` IS A `Device party`
      `the act` IS A `Device act`
      `the start` IS A DATE
      `the act has been done` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the act was done` IS A DATE
      `today` IS A DATE
      `the last day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Done in time or not`
`the outcome of` MEANS
    IF `the act has been done`
    THEN CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` (`day number of` `the start`) (LIST (WAITUNTIL (`day number of` `the day the act was done`)), (EVENT `the party` `the act` (`day number of` `the day the act was done`)))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `done in time`
         OTHERWISE `not done in time`
    ELSE CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` (`day number of` `the start`) (LIST (WAITUNTIL (`day number of` `today`)), (EVENT `the party` `the act` (`day number of` `today`)))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `still open until` `the last day`
         OTHERWISE `not done in time`

§§ `What the supplier or sponsor faces`

-- A record of the most a person faces under one provision. A zero means the provision is not reached on the facts.
-- Criminal offences need fault elements as well (Criminal Code Chapter 2, applied by s 41BK); a non-zero criminal figure
-- means only that the physical elements are made out on the facts given.
DECLARE `Most a person faces` HAS
    `provision` IS A STRING
    `imprisonment in months` IS A NUMBER
    `fine in penalty units` IS A NUMBER
    `strict liability fine in penalty units` IS A NUMBER
    `civil penalty in penalty units` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `why` IS A STRING
GIVETH A `Most a person faces`
`nothing under this provision` `why` MEANS
    `Most a person faces` WITH
        `provision`                              IS `why`
        `imprisonment in months`                 IS 0
        `fine in penalty units`                  IS 0
        `strict liability fine in penalty units` IS 0
        `civil penalty in penalty units`         IS 0

GIVEN `body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN, `for an individual` IS A NUMBER, `for a body corporate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the civil maximum` `body corporate` `for an individual` `for a body corporate` MEANS
    IF `body corporate` THEN `for a body corporate` ELSE `for an individual`

§ `Is my implant a medical device`

-- s 41BD(1)(a): "any instrument, apparatus, appliance, software, implant, reagent, material or other article ...
-- intended, by the person under whose name it is or is to be supplied, to be used for human beings for the purpose of"
-- (i) diagnosis, prevention, monitoring, prediction, prognosis, treatment or alleviation of disease; (ii) diagnosis,
-- monitoring, treatment, alleviation of or compensation for an injury or disability; (iii) investigation, replacement
-- or modification of the anatomy or of a physiological or pathological process or state; (iv) control or support of
-- conception; (v) in vitro examination of a specimen ...; "and that does not achieve its principal intended action in or
-- on the human body by pharmacological, immunological or metabolic means". The purpose is the one the supplier gives it
-- on the labelling, instructions, advertising or technical documentation (s 41BD(2)).
DECLARE `Intended purpose` IS ONE OF
    `diagnosing, preventing, monitoring, predicting or treating a disease`
    `diagnosing, monitoring, treating or compensating for an injury or disability`
    `investigating, replacing or modifying the anatomy or a bodily process`
    `controlling or supporting conception`
    `examining a specimen from the body in vitro`
    `none of these`

GIVEN `the purpose` IS AN `Intended purpose`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a s 41BD(1)(a) purpose` `the purpose` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the purpose`
    WHEN `none of these` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 41BD(1): a medical device is (a) the article above, (aa) an article the Secretary specifies under (2A), (ab) an
-- article in a class specified under (2B), (b) "an accessory" to such an article, or (c) "a system or procedure pack"
-- (s 41BF: two or more goods, at least one a medical device, to be interconnected or combined, or packaged together, for
-- use in a medical or surgical procedure). s 41BD(3): the Secretary may declare an article or class "not, for the
-- purposes of this Act, medical devices". The definition is closed ("A medical device is"): no limb, no device.
@export Is my implant (or other article used on me) a medical device under the Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 s 41BD?
GIVEN `it is an article` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an instrument, apparatus, appliance, software, implant, reagent, material or other article (a mesh, an implant, a tool)?
      `the purpose its supplier gives it` IS AN `Intended purpose` @desc The purpose its supplier gives it in its labelling, instructions, advertising or technical documentation. One of: diagnosing, preventing, monitoring, predicting or treating a disease; diagnosing, monitoring, treating or compensating for an injury or disability; investigating, replacing or modifying the anatomy or a bodily process; controlling or supporting conception; examining a specimen from the body in vitro; none of these
      `it works mainly by pharmacological, immunological or metabolic means` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it achieve its main intended action in or on your body by pharmacological, immunological or metabolic means (as a medicine does)?
      `the Secretary has specified it as a medical device` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of the Department of Health specified the article, or a class it belongs to, as medical devices (s 41BD(2A), (2B))?
      `it is an accessory to a medical device` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an accessory to an article that is a medical device?
      `it is a system or procedure pack` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it two or more goods, at least one a medical device, packaged together or to be combined for use in a medical or surgical procedure?
      `the Secretary has declared it not a medical device` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary declared the article, or a class it belongs to, not to be medical devices (s 41BD(3))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my implant a medical device` IF
        (NOT `the Secretary has declared it not a medical device`)
    AND (   (    `it is an article`
             AND `is a s 41BD(1)(a) purpose` `the purpose its supplier gives it`
             AND (NOT `it works mainly by pharmacological, immunological or metabolic means`))
         OR `the Secretary has specified it as a medical device`
         OR `it is an accessory to a medical device`
         OR `it is a system or procedure pack`)

§ `Who answers for my device`

-- s 3(1): "sponsor, in relation to therapeutic goods, means: (a) a person who exports, or arranges the exportation of,
-- the goods from Australia; or (b) a person who imports, or arranges the importation of, the goods into Australia; or
-- (c) a person who, in Australia, manufactures the goods, or arranges for another person to manufacture the goods, for
-- supply (whether in Australia or elsewhere); but does not include a person who ... exports, imports or manufactures the
-- goods; or ... arranges [that] ... on behalf of another person who, at the time ..., is a resident of, or is carrying on
-- business in, Australia."
DECLARE `What the company did with the device` IS ONE OF
    `imported it into Australia, or arranged its import`
    `manufactured it in Australia for supply, or arranged its manufacture`
    `exported it from Australia, or arranged its export`
    `none of these (for example, only distributed or implanted it)`

@export Is this company the sponsor of my device (s 3(1)), the person the Act holds to its duties?
GIVEN `what the company did` IS A `What the company did with the device` @desc What the company did with devices of this kind. One of: imported it into Australia, or arranged its import; manufactured it in Australia for supply, or arranged its manufacture; exported it from Australia, or arranged its export; none of these (for example, only distributed or implanted it)
      `it acted for someone in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company do this on behalf of another person who, at the time, lived or carried on business in Australia?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this company the sponsor of my device` IF
        (NOT `it acted for someone in Australia`)
    AND (CONSIDER `what the company did`
         WHEN `none of these (for example, only distributed or implanted it)` THEN FALSE
         OTHERWISE TRUE)

-- s 41BG(1): the manufacturer is "the person who is responsible for the design, production, packaging and labelling of
-- the device before it is supplied under the person's name". (2): if (1) does not apply, the person who, "with a view
-- to supplying the device under the person's name", assembles, packages, processes, fully refurbishes or labels it, or
-- assigns its purpose, "using ready-made products". (3): not a person who assembles or adapts it for an individual
-- patient, after another person has supplied it, without changing its intended purpose. (4): not a person in a class
-- the regulations prescribe. "Is the person who" is a closed definition: no limb, not the manufacturer.
@export Is this company the manufacturer of my device (s 41BG)?
GIVEN `it is responsible for design, production, packaging and labelling` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company responsible for the design, production, packaging and labelling of the device before it is supplied under its name (whether it does that work itself or has it done)?
      `it readies ready-made products for supply under its name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If not, does it, using ready-made products, assemble, package, process, fully refurbish or label the device, or assign it its purpose, with a view to supplying it under its own name?
      `it only adapted an already supplied device for one patient` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it only assemble or adapt, for an individual patient, a device someone else had already supplied, without changing the purpose that person gave it?
      `it is in a class the regulations exclude` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company in a class of persons the regulations say are not manufacturers (s 41BG(4))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this company the manufacturer of my device` IF
        (NOT `it is in a class the regulations exclude`)
    AND (NOT `it only adapted an already supplied device for one patient`)
    AND (   `it is responsible for design, production, packaging and labelling`
         OR `it readies ready-made products for supply under its name`)

§ `Was my device lawfully supplied to me`

-- s 3(1): "supply includes ... (d) supply by way of administration to, or application in the treatment of, a person".
-- Implanting a device in a patient is a supply of it, by the hospital or surgeon who implants it, as well as the
-- sponsor's earlier supply to the hospital. Each supply is asked about separately: one supplier, one supply, here.
--
-- s 41FM: the inclusion "commences on the day specified" in the certificate, and has effect "unless the kind of device
-- is suspended ... or until entry ... is cancelled". s 41GI: suspended devices "are taken ... not to be included in the
-- Register while the suspension has effect". s 41GQ: a cancellation under s 41GK or 41GL has effect on the day notice is
-- given, any other on a day "not earlier than 20 working days after" it; the day it took effect is asked, as the
-- Gazette or website notice (s 41GP) states it.
GIVEN `the day of supply` IS A DATE
      `the supplier is named on the entry` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the entry began on` IS A DATE
      `the entry was cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the cancellation took effect on` IS A DATE
      `the entry was suspended` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the suspension took effect on` IS A DATE
      `the suspension stopped having effect on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the entry in relation to the supplier was in effect on` IF
        `the supplier is named on the entry`
    AND `is on or after` `the day of supply` `the entry began on`
    AND (NOT (`the entry was cancelled` AND `is on or after` `the day of supply` `the cancellation took effect on`))
    AND (NOT (    `the entry was suspended`
              AND `is on or after` `the day of supply` `the suspension took effect on`
              AND `is before` `the day of supply` `the suspension stopped having effect on`))

-- s 41MI(1)(b), (4)(b), (5)(b) and s 41MIB(1)(b): none of these applies to the device: (i) "of a kind included in the
-- Register in relation to the person"; (ia) "covered by an exemption in force under section 41GS"; (ii) "an exempt
-- device"; (iii) "the subject of an approval under section 41HB or an authority under section 41HC"; (iv) "the subject of
-- an approval under subsection 41HD(1), (1A) or (2) that is held by the person".
@export Was my device covered (by its Register entry, an exemption, an approval or an authority) when this supplier supplied it to me (s 41MI(1)(b))?
GIVEN `the day it was supplied to me` IS A DATE @desc The day the supplier supplied the device to you (implanting it in you counts as supplying it), ISO 8601, e.g. 2014-03-15
      `the supplier is named on the entry` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the supplier the person in relation to whom the device's kind is included in the Australian Register of Therapeutic Goods (the sponsor named on the ARTG entry)?
      `the entry began on` IS A DATE @desc The day the ARTG entry began (its start date), ISO 8601
      `the entry was cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the ARTG entry been cancelled (for your device, if it was cancelled for some devices of the kind only)?
      `the cancellation took effect on` IS A DATE @desc If cancelled, the day the cancellation took effect, as the published notice says, ISO 8601 (any date if not cancelled)
      `the entry was suspended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the ARTG entry been suspended at any time (for your device)?
      `the suspension took effect on` IS A DATE @desc If suspended, the day the suspension took effect, ISO 8601 (any date if not suspended)
      `the suspension stopped having effect on` IS A DATE @desc If suspended, the first day the suspension no longer had effect (revoked or expired), or a day after today if it still has effect, ISO 8601
      `an emergency exemption under s 41GS covered it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the device of a kind covered by a Minister's emergency exemption in force under s 41GS?
      `it is an exempt device` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the device of a kind the regulations exempt from the Register requirement (an exempt device, such as a custom-made device)?
      `a special access approval or authorised prescriber authority covered it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the device the subject of a special access approval (s 41HB) or an authorised prescriber authority (s 41HC)?
      `the supplier held a shortage approval for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the supplier hold an approval under s 41HD (substitute for an unavailable device) for it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was my device covered when it was supplied to me` IF
        `the entry in relation to the supplier was in effect on` `the day it was supplied to me` `the supplier is named on the entry` `the entry began on` `the entry was cancelled` `the cancellation took effect on` `the entry was suspended` `the suspension took effect on` `the suspension stopped having effect on`
    OR  `an emergency exemption under s 41GS covered it`
    OR  `it is an exempt device`
    OR  `a special access approval or authorised prescriber authority covered it`
    OR  `the supplier held a shortage approval for it`

-- s 41MI(1): supplying a device in Australia none of whose (b) heads applies, where "(c) ... the use of the device has
-- resulted in, will result in, or is likely to result in, harm or injury to any person" (or would, if used): 5 years or
-- 4,000 penalty units. (7): (1) does not apply if the harm "did not, will not, or is not likely to, directly result from
-- (i) the quality, safety or performance of the medical device; or (ii) ... labelling or packaging ...; or (iii) the
-- improper use of the medical device". (4): the same without harm: 12 months or 1,000 penalty units. (5), (5A): the same,
-- strict liability, 100 penalty units. (6): "a defence ... if the defendant proves that the defendant was not the sponsor
-- of the device at the time". s 41MIB: civil penalty, 5,000 penalty units (individual) or 50,000 (body corporate);
-- (2): does not apply if the defendant proves it was not the sponsor.
-- s 41MK (wholesale supply of a device of a kind not on the Register, 120 penalty units) reaches only a supply to someone
-- who "is not the ultimate consumer": never the supply to the patient (NOTES.md finding 3).
@export What is the most this supplier faces for supplying my device when it was not covered by the Register (ss 41MI, 41MIB)?
GIVEN `the day it was supplied to me` IS A DATE @desc The day the supplier supplied the device to you (implanting it in you counts as supplying it), ISO 8601, e.g. 2014-03-15
      `my device was covered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the device covered when this supplier supplied it (its ARTG entry in the supplier's name was in effect, or an exemption, approval or authority covered it)? The question "Was my device covered when it was supplied to me" works this out.
      `its use has caused or is likely to cause harm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the use of the device caused, or will or is it likely to cause, harm or injury to anyone (or would it, if used)?
      `the harm comes directly from the device` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that harm come directly from the device's quality, safety or performance, its labelling or packaging, or its improper use?
      `the supplier was the sponsor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the supplier the sponsor of the device at the time of the supply (it imported it, or made it in Australia, for supply)?
      `the supplier is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the supplier a company or other body corporate (not an individual)?
GIVETH A `Most a person faces`
DECIDE `What does the supplier face for supplying my device uncovered` IS
    BRANCH IF `is before` `the day it was supplied to me` `the day Chapter 4 began`
           THEN `nothing under this provision` "Chapter 4 was not in force on the day of supply (it began on 4 October 2002); this encoding does not reach the law before it"
           IF `my device was covered`
           THEN `nothing under this provision` "none: the device was covered (s 41MI(1)(b))"
           IF NOT `the supplier was the sponsor`
           THEN `nothing under this provision` "none if the supplier proves it was not the sponsor at the time (s 41MI(6) defence; s 41MIB(2))"
           IF `its use has caused or is likely to cause harm` AND `the harm comes directly from the device`
           THEN `Most a person faces` WITH
                   `provision`                              IS "s 41MI(1) (harm), with s 41MI(5) strict liability and s 41MIB civil penalty"
                   `imprisonment in months`                 IS 60
                   `fine in penalty units`                  IS 4000
                   `strict liability fine in penalty units` IS 100
                   `civil penalty in penalty units`         IS `the civil maximum` `the supplier is a body corporate` 5000 50000
           OTHERWISE `Most a person faces` WITH
                   `provision`                              IS "s 41MI(4), with s 41MI(5) strict liability and s 41MIB civil penalty"
                   `imprisonment in months`                 IS 12
                   `fine in penalty units`                  IS 1000
                   `strict liability fine in penalty units` IS 100
                   `civil penalty in penalty units`         IS `the civil maximum` `the supplier is a body corporate` 5000 50000

-- s 41MA(5): supplying a medical device for use in Australia that "does not comply with the essential principles",
-- without the Secretary's consent, not covered by a s 41GS exemption, where its use has resulted in or is likely to
-- result in harm or injury, and the harm is "because the device does not comply": 5 years or 4,000 penalty units.
-- (8): the same without harm: 12 months or 1,000 penalty units. (8A), (8B): strict liability, 100 penalty units.
-- s 41MAA(2): civil penalty 5,000 (individual) or 50,000 (body corporate) penalty units.
-- s 41MB: ss 41MA and 41MAA "do not apply if" the device complies with a medical device standard that applies to it
-- and fails the essential principles only in parts the standard relates to. Whether it complies with the essential
-- principles (set by the regulations, s 41CA; not deposited) is asked. The deeming in s 41BH(2) does not reach Part 4-11;
-- s 41MB does the same work there.
@export What is the most this supplier faces for supplying my device if it did not comply with the essential principles (ss 41MA, 41MAA, 41MB)?
GIVEN `the day it was supplied to me` IS A DATE @desc The day the supplier supplied the device to you (implanting it in you counts as supplying it), ISO 8601
      `it did not comply with the essential principles` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the device fail to comply with the essential principles (the safety and performance requirements in the medical devices regulations), as a court or the regulator would find?
      `a standard excuses the failure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the device comply with a medical device standard that applies to it, and fail the essential principles only in parts that standard covers (s 41MB)?
      `the Secretary consented to the supply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had the Secretary consented to the supply of the non-complying device?
      `an emergency exemption under s 41GS covered it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the device of a kind covered by a Minister's emergency exemption in force under s 41GS?
      `its use has caused or is likely to cause harm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the use of the device caused, or will or is it likely to cause, harm or injury to anyone (or would it, if used)?
      `the harm is because it did not comply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that harm because the device did not comply with the essential principles?
      `the supplier is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the supplier a company or other body corporate (not an individual)?
GIVETH A `Most a person faces`
DECIDE `What does the supplier face for supplying my device non-compliant` IS
    BRANCH IF `is before` `the day it was supplied to me` `the day Chapter 4 began`
           THEN `nothing under this provision` "Chapter 4 was not in force on the day of supply (it began on 4 October 2002); this encoding does not reach the law before it"
           IF NOT `it did not comply with the essential principles`
           THEN `nothing under this provision` "none: the device complied with the essential principles (s 41MA(5)(b))"
           IF `a standard excuses the failure`
           THEN `nothing under this provision` "none: ss 41MA and 41MAA do not apply (s 41MB, a matter the supplier must raise or prove)"
           IF `the Secretary consented to the supply` OR `an emergency exemption under s 41GS covered it`
           THEN `nothing under this provision` "none: the Secretary consented, or a s 41GS exemption covered the device (s 41MA(5)(c), (ca))"
           IF `its use has caused or is likely to cause harm` AND `the harm is because it did not comply`
           THEN `Most a person faces` WITH
                   `provision`                              IS "s 41MA(5) (harm), with s 41MA(8A) strict liability and s 41MAA(2) civil penalty"
                   `imprisonment in months`                 IS 60
                   `fine in penalty units`                  IS 4000
                   `strict liability fine in penalty units` IS 100
                   `civil penalty in penalty units`         IS `the civil maximum` `the supplier is a body corporate` 5000 50000
           OTHERWISE `Most a person faces` WITH
                   `provision`                              IS "s 41MA(8), with s 41MA(8A) strict liability and s 41MAA(2) civil penalty"
                   `imprisonment in months`                 IS 12
                   `fine in penalty units`                  IS 1000
                   `strict liability fine in penalty units` IS 100
                   `civil penalty in penalty units`         IS `the civil maximum` `the supplier is a body corporate` 5000 50000

§ `Recall and warnings about my device`

-- s 41KA(1): the Secretary "may, in writing, impose requirements" on the person in the table's third column if a
-- circumstance in the second column occurs. The sponsor named on the entry ("the person in relation to whom it is
-- included in the Register") is the person for items 1 (supplied while included, Secretary satisfied it does not comply
-- with the essential principles), 2 (Secretary satisfied neither the conformity assessment procedures nor comparable
-- requirements were applied), 5B (it appears to the Secretary its quality, safety or performance is unacceptable), 6
-- (suspended) and 7 (entry cancelled). The power is the Secretary's: TRUE means it is open, not that it was used.
@export Can the sponsor named on my device's Register entry be required to recall it, or to warn the public or patients about it (s 41KA, items 1, 2, 5B, 6, 7)?
GIVEN `it was supplied while on the Register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the device supplied while its kind was included in the Australian Register of Therapeutic Goods?
      `the Secretary is satisfied it does not meet the essential principles` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Secretary satisfied that devices of that kind do not comply with the essential principles?
      `the Secretary is satisfied conformity assessment was not applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Secretary satisfied that neither the conformity assessment procedures nor comparable overseas requirements were applied to devices of that kind?
      `it appears to the Secretary its quality, safety or performance is unacceptable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the Secretary that the quality, safety or performance of devices of that kind is unacceptable?
      `the entry has been suspended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the kind of device been suspended from the Register?
      `the entry has been cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the kind of device's entry been cancelled from the Register?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the sponsor be required to recall or warn about my device` IF
        (    `it was supplied while on the Register`
         AND (   `the Secretary is satisfied it does not meet the essential principles`
              OR `the Secretary is satisfied conformity assessment was not applied`
              OR `it appears to the Secretary its quality, safety or performance is unacceptable`))
    OR  `the entry has been suspended`
    OR  `the entry has been cancelled`

-- s 41KA(1), items 3 and 4 (supplied as an exempt device, or under a s 41HB approval, s 41HC authority or s 41HD
-- approval, and the Secretary is satisfied it does not comply with the essential principles, or that conformity
-- assessment was not applied), 4A (the Secretary is satisfied the supply contravenes a s 9K prohibition or its
-- conditions), 5 (supplied while "not included in the Register" and not covered by a s 41GS exemption, an exempt device,
-- or a s 41HB, 41HC or 41HD approval or authority), 5A (supplied under a s 41GS exemption and the Secretary is satisfied
-- it is not fit for its intended purpose) and 8 (counterfeit goods): "The person supplying the kind of medical device".
@export Can the person who supplied my device be required to recall it, or to warn the public or patients about it (s 41KA, items 3, 4, 4A, 5, 5A, 8)?
GIVEN `its kind was on the Register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc When it was supplied, was the kind of device included in the Australian Register of Therapeutic Goods (in anyone's name)?
      `an emergency exemption under s 41GS covered it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it supplied while covered by a Minister's emergency exemption under s 41GS?
      `it was supplied as exempt or under an approval or authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it supplied as an exempt device, or under a special access approval (s 41HB), an authorised prescriber authority (s 41HC) or a shortage approval (s 41HD)?
      `the Secretary is satisfied it does not meet the essential principles` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Secretary satisfied that devices of that kind do not comply with the essential principles?
      `the Secretary is satisfied conformity assessment was not applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Secretary satisfied that neither the conformity assessment procedures nor comparable overseas requirements were applied to devices of that kind?
      `the Secretary is satisfied the supply broke a s 9K prohibition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Secretary satisfied that the supply contravened a prohibition (or its conditions) in force under s 9K?
      `the Secretary is satisfied it is not fit for its purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Secretary satisfied that the device is not fit to be used for its intended purpose (relevant only under a s 41GS exemption)?
      `it is counterfeit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the device counterfeit goods (s 42E)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the supplier be required to recall or warn about my device` IF
        (    `it was supplied as exempt or under an approval or authority`
         AND (   `the Secretary is satisfied it does not meet the essential principles`
              OR `the Secretary is satisfied conformity assessment was not applied`))
    OR  `the Secretary is satisfied the supply broke a s 9K prohibition`
    OR  (    (NOT `its kind was on the Register`)
         AND (NOT `an emergency exemption under s 41GS covered it`)
         AND (NOT `it was supplied as exempt or under an approval or authority`))
    OR  (`an emergency exemption under s 41GS covered it` AND `the Secretary is satisfied it is not fit for its purpose`)
    OR  `it is counterfeit`

-- s 41KA(2)(a): a requirement may be "to take specified steps ... to recall medical devices of that kind that have been
-- distributed"; (3): it may be limited to some devices of the kind. (4): "A requirement to recall medical devices under
-- this section does not apply to a medical device that cannot be recalled because it has been administered to, or
-- applied in the treatment of, a person." A flat negative: an implanted device is never reached by a recall. The
-- requirements in (2)(b)-(e) (to inform the public or a class of persons, to publish, to tell the Secretary who was
-- supplied) are not limited by (4).
@export Does a recall requirement under s 41KA reach my own device, now that it has been implanted or used in my treatment (s 41KA(4))?
GIVEN `a recall requirement has been imposed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary imposed a requirement under s 41KA to recall devices of your device's kind?
      `the requirement is limited to devices other than mine` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the requirement limited to some devices of the kind (for example certain batches) that do not include yours?
      `my device has been implanted or used in my treatment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your device been implanted in you, administered to you or applied in your treatment?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does a recall requirement reach my device` IF
        `a recall requirement has been imposed`
    AND (NOT `the requirement is limited to devices other than mine`)
    AND (NOT `my device has been implanted or used in my treatment`)

-- s 41KC(1): breaching a s 41KA requirement where the act or omission "has resulted in, will result in, or is likely to
-- result in, harm or injury to any person": 5 years or 4,000 penalty units. (4): without harm, 12 months or 1,000
-- penalty units. (5), (6): strict liability, 100 penalty units. s 41KCA: civil penalty 5,000 (individual) or 50,000
-- (body corporate) penalty units.
@export What is the most a person faces for not complying with a recall or warning requirement about my device (ss 41KC, 41KCA)?
GIVEN `a requirement was imposed on them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Secretary impose a requirement under s 41KA (to recall, warn, publish or report) on that person?
      `they did not comply with it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did they do or fail to do something that breached the requirement?
      `the breach has caused or is likely to cause harm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the breach caused, or will or is it likely to cause, harm or injury to anyone?
      `they are a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that person a company or other body corporate (not an individual)?
GIVETH A `Most a person faces`
DECIDE `What does a person face for not complying with a recall or warning requirement` IS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`a requirement was imposed on them` AND `they did not comply with it`)
           THEN `nothing under this provision` "none: no s 41KA requirement on that person was breached"
           IF `the breach has caused or is likely to cause harm`
           THEN `Most a person faces` WITH
                   `provision`                              IS "s 41KC(1) (harm), with s 41KC(5) strict liability and s 41KCA civil penalty"
                   `imprisonment in months`                 IS 60
                   `fine in penalty units`                  IS 4000
                   `strict liability fine in penalty units` IS 100
                   `civil penalty in penalty units`         IS `the civil maximum` `they are a body corporate` 5000 50000
           OTHERWISE `Most a person faces` WITH
                   `provision`                              IS "s 41KC(4), with s 41KC(5) strict liability and s 41KCA civil penalty"
                   `imprisonment in months`                 IS 12
                   `fine in penalty units`                  IS 1000
                   `strict liability fine in penalty units` IS 100
                   `civil penalty in penalty units`         IS `the civil maximum` `they are a body corporate` 5000 50000

§ `What the sponsor had to report about problems with my device`

-- s 41MP(2) and s 41MPA(2), in the same words: information (a) relating to (i) "any malfunction or deterioration in the
-- characteristics or performance of the kind of device", (ii) "any inadequacy in the design, production, labelling,
-- instructions for use or advertising materials", or (iii) "any use in accordance with, or contrary to, the use intended
-- by the manufacturer", "that might lead, or might have led, to the death of a patient or a user of the device, or to a
-- serious deterioration in his or her state of health"; (b) "any technical or medical reason for a malfunction or
-- deterioration ... that has led the manufacturer to take steps to recall devices of that kind"; (c) information "that
-- indicates that a device of that kind does not comply with the essential principles"; (d) information that a
-- certificate used for the Register application "has been restricted, suspended, revoked or is no longer in effect".
-- "Information of the following kinds" closes the list.
DECLARE `What the information is about` IS ONE OF
    `a malfunction or deterioration of the device`
    `an inadequacy in its design, production, labelling, instructions or advertising`
    `a use of the device, as the manufacturer intended or not`
    `the technical or medical reason for a malfunction that led the manufacturer to recall`
    `that the device does not comply with the essential principles`
    `that a certificate used for its Register application was restricted, suspended or revoked`
    `something else`

GIVEN `what it is about` IS A `What the information is about`
      `it might lead to death or serious deterioration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the information is of a s 41MP(2) kind` IF
    CONSIDER `what it is about`
    WHEN `a malfunction or deterioration of the device` THEN `it might lead to death or serious deterioration`
    WHEN `an inadequacy in its design, production, labelling, instructions or advertising` THEN `it might lead to death or serious deterioration`
    WHEN `a use of the device, as the manufacturer intended or not` THEN `it might lead to death or serious deterioration`
    WHEN `the technical or medical reason for a malfunction that led the manufacturer to recall` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `that the device does not comply with the essential principles` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `that a certificate used for its Register application was restricted, suspended or revoked` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `something else` THEN FALSE

@export Was what the sponsor learned about my device's kind information it had to report to the regulator (s 41MP(2), s 41MPA(2))?
GIVEN `what the information is about` IS A `What the information is about` @desc What the information is about. One of: a malfunction or deterioration of the device; an inadequacy in its design, production, labelling, instructions or advertising; a use of the device, as the manufacturer intended or not; the technical or medical reason for a malfunction that led the manufacturer to recall; that the device does not comply with the essential principles; that a certificate used for its Register application was restricted, suspended or revoked; something else
      `it might lead to death or serious deterioration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Might the malfunction, inadequacy or use lead (or have led) to a patient's or user's death, or a serious deterioration in their health?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was it information the sponsor had to report` IF
    `the information is of a s 41MP(2) kind` `what the information is about` `it might lead to death or serious deterioration`

-- The duty arises only for "a person in relation to whom a kind of medical device is included in the Register"
-- (s 41MP(1)(a), s 41MPA(1)(a)) and only for information of a s 41MP(2) kind.
@export Did the sponsor of my device report what it learned to the regulator in time (ss 41FN(3)(d), 41MP, 41MPA)?
GIVEN `the kind is on the Register in the sponsor's name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your device's kind included in the Australian Register of Therapeutic Goods in relation to the sponsor?
      `what the information is about` IS A `What the information is about` @desc What the information is about. One of: a malfunction or deterioration of the device; an inadequacy in its design, production, labelling, instructions or advertising; a use of the device, as the manufacturer intended or not; the technical or medical reason for a malfunction that led the manufacturer to recall; that the device does not comply with the essential principles; that a certificate used for its Register application was restricted, suspended or revoked; something else
      `it might lead to death or serious deterioration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Might the malfunction, inadequacy or use lead (or have led) to a patient's or user's death, or a serious deterioration in their health?
      `the day the sponsor became aware` IS A DATE @desc The day the sponsor became aware of the information, ISO 8601
      `the days the regulations allow` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days the Therapeutic Goods (Medical Devices) Regulations allow the sponsor after becoming aware (for example 2, 10 or 30, depending on how serious it is)
      `the sponsor has reported it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the sponsor given the information to the Secretary (the TGA)?
      `the day it reported` IS A DATE @desc If it has, the day it gave the information, ISO 8601 (any date if it has not)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date, ISO 8601
GIVETH A `Done in time or not`
DECIDE `Did the sponsor report in time` IS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`the kind is on the Register in the sponsor's name` AND `the information is of a s 41MP(2) kind` `what the information is about` `it might lead to death or serious deterioration`)
           THEN `there is no such duty on these facts`
           IF `the sponsor has reported it` AND `is before` `the day it reported` `the day the sponsor became aware`
           THEN `done in time`
           OTHERWISE `the outcome of` (`ss 41MP, 41MPA -- the sponsor must give the information to the Secretary within the period in the regulations` (`day number of` (`the last day of` `the days the regulations allow` `days after` `the day the sponsor became aware`) MINUS `day number of` `the day the sponsor became aware`)) `the sponsor` `give the information to the Secretary` `the day the sponsor became aware` `the sponsor has reported it` `the day it reported` `today` (`the last day of` `the days the regulations allow` `days after` `the day the sponsor became aware`)

-- s 41MP(1): the offence needs the sponsor to know "that particular information is information of a kind mentioned in
-- subsection (2)": 12 months or 1,000 penalty units. s 41MPA(1): the civil penalty needs no knowledge: 3,000 penalty
-- units (individual) or 30,000 (body corporate). s 41MPB: a court may relieve the sponsor wholly or partly if it "has a
-- reasonable excuse" and "ought fairly to be excused" (a judgment left to the court; the figure is the maximum before
-- any relief). s 41GN(1)(d): a contravention is a ground on which the Secretary may cancel the entry.
@export What is the most the sponsor faces for not reporting in time what it learned about my device (ss 41MP, 41MPA)?
GIVEN `it did not report in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the sponsor fail to report the information in time? The question "Did the sponsor report in time" works this out.
      `the sponsor knew it was reportable information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the sponsor know the information was of a kind it had to report?
      `the sponsor is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the sponsor a company or other body corporate (not an individual)?
GIVETH A `Most a person faces`
DECIDE `What does the sponsor face for not reporting` IS
    BRANCH IF NOT `it did not report in time`
           THEN `nothing under this provision` "none: no failure to report in time"
           IF `the sponsor knew it was reportable information`
           THEN `Most a person faces` WITH
                   `provision`                              IS "s 41MP(1) offence and s 41MPA civil penalty (the court may relieve under s 41MPB); a ground to cancel the entry (s 41GN(1)(d))"
                   `imprisonment in months`                 IS 12
                   `fine in penalty units`                  IS 1000
                   `strict liability fine in penalty units` IS 0
                   `civil penalty in penalty units`         IS `the civil maximum` `the sponsor is a body corporate` 3000 30000
           OTHERWISE `Most a person faces` WITH
                   `provision`                              IS "s 41MPA civil penalty only (the s 41MP offence needs knowledge; the court may relieve under s 41MPB); a ground to cancel the entry (s 41GN(1)(d))"
                   `imprisonment in months`                 IS 0
                   `fine in penalty units`                  IS 0
                   `strict liability fine in penalty units` IS 0
                   `civil penalty in penalty units`         IS `the civil maximum` `the sponsor is a body corporate` 3000 30000

§ `What the hospital must report about what happened to me` -- arises only if a device harmed you, or nearly did, in a hospital

-- s 3(1): "healthcare facility means: (a) a public hospital; or (b) a private hospital; or (c) any other facility
-- prescribed by regulations". "reportable medical device means a medical device of a kind prescribed by regulations".
DECLARE `Kind of facility` IS ONE OF
    `a public hospital`
    `a private hospital`
    `another facility the regulations prescribe`
    `none of these (for example a clinic that is not prescribed)`

DECLARE `What happened at the facility` IS ONE OF
    `the device was used on me there and caused my death or a serious deterioration in my health`
    `someone there stopped the device being used, and its use would have caused death or a serious deterioration`
    `I was treated there for a serious deterioration in my health caused by the device`
    `none of these`

-- s 41JM(1): the chief executive officer of a healthcare facility "must give a report to the Secretary if subsection (2),
-- (3) or (4) applies". (2): a reportable device "is used in the facility" and its use "has resulted in the death, or a
-- serious deterioration in the health, of a person while the device is used in the facility". (3): it "is not used in the
-- facility because of the intervention of a person in the facility" and its use "would result in, or would be likely to
-- result in" death or serious deterioration. (4): "a health practitioner provides treatment to a person in the facility
-- for a serious deterioration in the health of the person" and the use of a reportable device "has resulted in" it.
-- (7): (1) "does not apply if" the chief executive officer has reported the matters to the chief executive officer of
-- the Australian Commission on Safety and Quality in Health Care, the head of a State or Territory health department, or
-- a prescribed person. (8): civil penalty, 30 penalty units. The report's time and manner are prescribed (6): not
-- encoded.
--
-- Part 4-8A was added by the Therapeutic Goods Amendment (2022 Measures No. 1) Act 2023 (No. 10, 2023), assented to
-- 21 March 2023; its schedules began on 22 March 2023 (schs 3-10, 12), 21 June 2023 (sch 2), 21 September 2023 (sch 11)
-- and 21 March 2025 (sch 1). The deposited endnotes do not say which schedule added Part 4-8A. So: before 22 March 2023
-- the duty did not exist (JUST FALSE); from 21 March 2025 it did, whatever the schedule; between, NOTHING (NOTES.md
-- finding 7).
`the earliest day Part 4-8A could have begun` MEANS `the date` 22 3 2023
`the day every schedule of No. 10, 2023 had begun` MEANS `the date` 21 3 2025

@export Must the hospital report to the regulator what a medical device did to me (s 41JM)? No answer between 22 March 2023 and 20 March 2025, when the start of the duty cannot be told from the deposited text.
GIVEN `the day it happened` IS A DATE @desc The day the device was used on you, or stopped, or you were treated for the deterioration, ISO 8601
      `the kind of facility` IS A `Kind of facility` @desc Where it happened. One of: a public hospital; a private hospital; another facility the regulations prescribe; none of these (for example a clinic that is not prescribed)
      `the device is a reportable medical device` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the device of a kind the regulations prescribe as a reportable medical device?
      `what happened` IS A `What happened at the facility` @desc What happened. One of: the device was used on me there and caused my death or a serious deterioration in my health; someone there stopped the device being used, and its use would have caused death or a serious deterioration; I was treated there for a serious deterioration in my health caused by the device; none of these
      `it was already reported elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the facility's chief executive already reported it to the Australian Commission on Safety and Quality in Health Care, the State or Territory health department, or another person the regulations name?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the hospital report what happened to me` IS
    BRANCH IF `is before` `the day it happened` `the earliest day Part 4-8A could have begun`
           THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `is before` `the day it happened` `the day every schedule of No. 10, 2023 had begun`
           THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST (    (CONSIDER `the kind of facility`
                           WHEN `none of these (for example a clinic that is not prescribed)` THEN FALSE
                           OTHERWISE TRUE)
                      AND `the device is a reportable medical device`
                      AND (CONSIDER `what happened`
                           WHEN `none of these` THEN FALSE
                           OTHERWISE TRUE)
                      AND (NOT `it was already reported elsewhere`))

§ `A device supplied to me under an authorisation` -- arises only if a health practitioner supplied you a device not on the Register under rules made under s 41HC(6)

-- s 41HC(6B): a person authorised by s 41HC(6) rules who supplies a device of that kind in accordance with the rules
-- "must (c) notify the supply to the Secretary; and (d) do so within 28 days after the supply". (6E), (6F): failing is
-- a strict liability offence, 10 penalty units. (6FA): the offence does not apply if a health practitioner notifies
-- "on behalf of the person" within 28 days: a notification by either counts here.
@export Did the health practitioner who supplied my device under s 41HC(6) rules notify the regulator within 28 days (s 41HC(6B))?
GIVEN `it was supplied under s 41HC(6) rules` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the device supplied to you by a health practitioner authorised to do so by rules the Minister made under s 41HC(6)?
      `the day it was supplied to me` IS A DATE @desc The day it was supplied to you (implanting it counts as supplying it), ISO 8601
      `the supply has been notified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the supply been notified to the Secretary (the TGA), by the practitioner or by a health practitioner on their behalf?
      `the day it was notified` IS A DATE @desc If it has, the day it was notified, ISO 8601 (any date if not)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date, ISO 8601
GIVETH A `Done in time or not`
DECIDE `Was the supply to me notified in time` IS
    BRANCH IF NOT `it was supplied under s 41HC(6) rules`
           THEN `there is no such duty on these facts`
           IF `the supply has been notified` AND `is before` `the day it was notified` `the day it was supplied to me`
           THEN `not done in time`
           OTHERWISE `the outcome of` (`s 41HC(6B) -- the health practitioner must notify the supply within 28 days after it` (`day number of` (`the last day of` 28 `days after` `the day it was supplied to me`) MINUS `day number of` `the day it was supplied to me`)) `the health practitioner` `notify the supply to the Secretary` `the day it was supplied to me` `the supply has been notified` `the day it was notified` `today` (`the last day of` 28 `days after` `the day it was supplied to me`)
